{"status":"Error","code":"InvalidParameter","error":"The Item Tracking domain is turned off for this company. Turn it on from Inventory Setup.","nextStep":"Ask an administrator with the Inv. Posting Gate permission set to turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page. Data.Records.Set cannot change this setup.","hint":"For usage details, call the \"Help.Implementation.Get\" message type with subject \"Inventory.TrackingAvailability.Get\". Always read the help before calling a message type."}

--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "subject": {
      "use": "optional",
      "forms": [
        "guid",
        "item no."
      ],
      "description": "The subject is the SystemId or No. of the Item; data selects the same item when subject is blank."
    },
    "dataRequired": false,
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json"
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "subject",
      "form": "guid",
      "description": "The SystemId of the Item."
    },
    {
      "source": "subject",
      "form": "item no.",
      "description": "The No. of the Item; it takes precedence over the item identifiers in data."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.itemNo",
      "form": "item no.",
      "description": "The No. of the Item, used when subject is blank."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.itemId, data.id, data.systemId, data.recordSystemId",
      "form": "guid",
      "description": "The SystemId of the Item, tried in this order after itemNo. Document line SystemIds are not accepted."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.tableView",
      "form": "table view",
      "description": "An Item table view; the first matching item is read, so filter to one item for an exact selection."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "itemNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Item number; subject takes precedence."
    },
    {
      "name": "itemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Item SystemId."
    },
    {
      "name": "id",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Item SystemId alias."
    },
    {
      "name": "systemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Item SystemId alias; document-line selectors are not supported by this operation."
    },
    {
      "name": "recordSystemId",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Item SystemId alias."
    },
    {
      "name": "tableView",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Business Central Item table view in SetView syntax. Used after subject and item identifiers; reads availability for the first matching item. Filter to one item for an exact selection."
    },
    {
      "name": "locationFilter",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Business Central location filter."
    },
    {
      "name": "locationCode",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Exact location code; intersects locationFilter."
    },
    {
      "name": "variantCode",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Exact variant code, including blank."
    },
    {
      "name": "lotNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Exact lot number, including blank."
    },
    {
      "name": "serialNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Exact serial number, including blank."
    },
    {
      "name": "packageNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Exact package number, including blank."
    },
    {
      "name": "skip",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Number of rows to skip; default 0."
    },
    {
      "name": "take",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Page size 1..10000; default 100."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success after the operation completes."
      },
      {
        "name": "itemNo",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Selected item."
      },
      {
        "name": "availability",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "One group per location, variant, lot, serial and package of open positive tracked item ledger entries. Quantities are base units; availability subtracts reserved from remaining quantity.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "lotNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The lot number of the group; blank when the group has none."
          },
          {
            "name": "serialNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The serial number of the group; blank when the group has none."
          },
          {
            "name": "packageNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The package number of the group; blank when the group has none."
          },
          {
            "name": "locationCode",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The location code of the group."
          },
          {
            "name": "variantCode",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The variant code of the group."
          },
          {
            "name": "expirationDate",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The expiration date in YYYY-MM-DD form when the item tracking code uses expiration dates and the grouped entries agree; otherwise blank."
          },
          {
            "name": "inventory",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The remaining quantity of the group in the base unit of measure."
          },
          {
            "name": "remainingQuantity",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The remaining quantity of the group; the same as inventory."
          },
          {
            "name": "qtyReserved",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The quantity of the group that is reserved, in the base unit of measure."
          },
          {
            "name": "availableQuantity",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The remaining quantity less the reserved quantity."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "noOfLines",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "Rows returned after skip and take."
      },
      {
        "name": "totalNoOfLines",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "All matching rows before paging."
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "error": "itemNo must be specified.",
      "when": "data.itemNo was not sent or is blank.",
      "fix": "Send the item number in data.itemNo."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "A source object, identifier, number, date, filter or array has an invalid type or range.",
      "fix": "Use the declared JSON types and valid ranges."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "The source, pairing or tracking values are unsupported, quantity is unavailable, the source is closed, or the company domain is disabled.",
      "fix": "Correct the selection and quantity; check Inventory Setup and native source rules."
    },
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "when": "A requested item identifier cannot be resolved by Foundation.",
      "fix": "Correct the item selector; no tracked stock is a successful empty page."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The caller lacks required domain or native table permissions.",
      "fix": "Ask an administrator for the required permissions."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "Native item selection or filter error.",
      "when": "Foundation rejects the item selector or a native filter cannot be evaluated.",
      "fix": "Correct the item selection and Business Central filter syntax."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "read",
    "changes": "Nothing is changed. Reads the open tracked item ledger entries of the item and the quantity reserved against them.",
    "idempotent": true,
    "permissionSet": "Bifrost Read-Only",
    "writes": false
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Tracking.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Read the tracking rows (ledger entries, reservations and specifications) of an item or a document line instead of availability per lot."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Tracking.Assign",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Create a tracking specification instead of reading availability."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Tracking.Delete",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Delete a tracking specification instead of reading availability."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Read the reservations of the item when you need the demand behind qtyReserved."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Read an owned lot availability",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.TrackingAvailability.Get",
        "data": {
          "itemNo": "OWNED-ITEM",
          "lotNo": "OWNED-LOT",
          "take": 100
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "itemNo": "OWNED-ITEM",
        "availability": [
          {
            "lotNo": "OWNED-LOT",
            "serialNo": "",
            "packageNo": "",
            "locationCode": "BLUE",
            "variantCode": "",
            "expirationDate": "",
            "inventory": 2,
            "remainingQuantity": 2,
            "qtyReserved": 0,
            "availableQuantity": 2
          }
        ],
        "noOfLines": 1,
        "totalNoOfLines": 1
      },
      "description": "Create your own compatible item, document line and stock first; replace illustrative identifiers with those owned records. Normal licensing and permissions apply."
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Reads tracked inventory, reserved quantities and availability by location and variant.",
  "notes": "Read only. Groups open positive tracked item ledger entries by location, variant, lot, serial and package. All quantities use base units; availableQuantity equals remainingQuantity minus qtyReserved. expirationDate is the native entry date only with Use Expiration Dates enabled, and blank for undated or disagreeing grouped entries. No matching stock returns a successful empty page. Filters apply before paging."
}

## Errors and warnings
An error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.
When a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.
Request values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.
Request values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `"1234.56"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.
Answers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.
Both success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.
`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {"type":"Memory.User.Set","strict":true,"data":{"memory":"test","memry":"typo"}} is refused.
`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.
Feature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.
A message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.
`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is "no concurrent lock on the same records"; `nextStep` is "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed." Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.
Codes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.
